            "bug_id": 19200,
            "text": "On builds without libdeflate, memDecompress(type = \"gzip\") never returns for a gzip or zlib stream that ends prematurely: every pass of its retry loop R_alloc()s another output buffer of the same size, so the call exhausts memory, or spins at zero bytes if nothing was decoded at all. Found by OSS-Fuzz (testcases 5726025607348224, 6383420146778112 and 6066205270802432, all the same cause).\n\nReproducible example (r90638 configured with ac_cv_header_libdeflate_h=no; the libdeflate build gives 'internal error 1' immediately in both cases):\n\n  memDecompress(as.raw(c(0x78, 0x9c, 0x0a, 0x20)), \"gzip\")  # zlib header + 2 bytes: hangs\n  z <- memCompress(raw(1000), \"gzip\")\n  memDecompress(z[-length(z)], \"gzip\")                      # allocates until the vector limit\n\nAnalysis:\n\nR_uncompress() in gzio.h writes stream.total_out through destLen on every return, not only on success. do_memDecompress() passes outlen by reference and treats Z_BUF_ERROR as \"buffer too small\", doubling outlen and retrying. inflate() also returns Z_BUF_ERROR when the input runs out mid-stream, and then total_out is independent of the buffer size, so the doubled value is the same on every pass and the loop never terminates. The libdeflate branch is a separate loop keyed on LIBDEFLATE_INSUFFICIENT_SPACE and is not affected.\n\nProposed patch: attached as memdecompress-truncated-gzip.diff. It keeps the size of the buffer just allocated in its own variable, grows only when Z_BUF_ERROR comes back with that buffer completely filled, and otherwise falls through to the existing error (-5 for truncated input). A regression test in reg-tests-1e.R asserts an error for both inputs above and for a gzip member without its trailer; it passes with and without libdeflate, and make test-Reg passes.\n\nThe patch is also submitted as https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/357, where CI results can be seen."
          },
